# tools/p/plant_witness.rish -- a plant is a claim about a file, and this proves the claim can red.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. A control breaks a module on purpose and watches its witness refuse. The break is
# almost always a `sed` naming one literal line of the real source. That naming is a claim -- "this
# line, spelled this way, stands in that file today" -- and on 20260906 a type in
# mantra/src/diff.rye changed from u32 to LineId while tools/fixtures/m/mantra_diff_control.sh went
# on naming the elder spelling. The sed matched nothing, the pen was copied byte for byte, and the
# phase built and ran the UNMUTATED module. It exited 0, which is the reading a law that holds
# gives. Every phase in that control asserted what the pen does AFTER the break; not one asserted
# the break landed (REDS %519).
#
# Three hands had already met this fault and each repaired it locally, in its own spelling. This
# rung proves the one implementation they can all import instead.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal, by tools/fixtures/p/plant_control.sh.
#   Thirty behaviors on real files in a throwaway pen, each function shown from BOTH sides.
#   plant_landed reads a difference, reads its absence by name, and refuses an absent file.
#   plant_write lands, leaves the source alone, and on a stale line writes NO destination at all --
#     so a caller ignoring the return value still cannot build an unmutated pen and read it as a
#     break, which is the exact shape %519 booked.
#   plant_write refuses an empty program and a program sed itself rejects, each by its own word.
#     The second matters more than it looks: a rejected program leaves a partial or empty file,
#     which DIFFERS from the source, so a bare byte comparison would call that plant landed.
#   plant_apply rewrites in place, keeps the file's exec bit (it writes through the original inode,
#     where `mv` would carry the temporary's mode -- .claude/rules/exec-bit.md), leaves no
#     temporary behind, and leaves a stale plant's file byte-identical.
#   plant_write to a destination that does not exist yet keeps the mode too, by seeding it with
#     `cp` rather than reading the mode back -- `stat`'s field-format flag is GNU's `-c` and BSD's
#     `-f`, one more dialect question, and `shell_dialect` holds `stat -c` at zero.
#   The load-bearing leg: the same helper with the byte comparison stripped out of plant_apply
#     reads a no-op plant as LANDED. A helper that answered "landed" about everything would pass
#     every welcome leg above; that failing reading standing green beside the real one is what
#     tells a working check from one that has merely started saying yes.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED RATHER THAN GATED: adoption. tools/fixtures/p/plant_adoption_scan.sh counts the
# tracked controls that source the helper, and the floor below only ever RISES -- the mirror of
# this tree's usual ratchet, because the population being counted is the good one.
#
# WHY ADOPTION AND NOT EXPOSURE. Counting the controls that plant without checking needs a rule for
# telling a plant from a fixture build, and every candidate rule misreads real files today.
# Measured at e567cbc128 over the seven controls carrying `cmp -s`: four use it to prove a plant
# landed, and three use it to prove a file did NOT change. Reading the word `planted` instead fails
# from the other side -- two of those three carry it, once for pen rows the control wrote itself
# and once in header prose. One operator, three claims. Sourcing a file is exact.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That a control's plants are the RIGHT plants, or that its witness bites for
# the right reason. Only that a plant which changed nothing says so, by name, before any number is
# read.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/p/plant_witness.rish

say "plant: Language EN -- a plant that plants nothing reads exactly like a law that holds."
say "plant: Style Gauge, Meter -- each function shown from both sides, the refusal named."
say "plant: Lens TAME -- safety first: the check that asserts the defect is the load-bearing one."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/plant_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "plant: the control must complete -- read its own lines"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "faults=0" else "plant: every behavior must be satisfied"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "plant: the control must balance before it is believed"

# The reading alone, both ways.
assert control.out contains "OK   landed_on_difference" else "plant: two differing files must read as a landed plant"
assert control.out contains "OK   landed_on_identical" else "plant: two identical files must read as a plant that landed nothing"
assert control.out contains "OK   identical_names_the_word" else "plant: the refusal must name plant_matched_nothing, a word rather than a number"
assert control.out contains "OK   absent_names_its_own_word" else "plant: an absent file must be told apart from a stale line"

# plant_write: the destination is the safety, not only the return value.
assert control.out contains "OK   write_lands" else "plant: a program that matches must rewrite the file"
assert control.out contains "OK   write_actually_changed_the_bytes" else "plant: the rewrite must reach the bytes, not only the exit code"
assert control.out contains "OK   write_refuses_a_stale_line" else "plant: a program matching nothing must refuse"
assert control.out contains "OK   refused_write_leaves_no_destination" else "plant: a refused plant must write no destination, so an ignored return value still cannot pass"
assert control.out contains "OK   empty_program_names_its_own_word" else "plant: an empty program is a caller fault and must be named apart"
assert control.out contains "OK   write_refuses_a_program_sed_rejects" else "plant: a program sed rejects leaves a file that DIFFERS, so the exit code must be read"
assert control.out contains "OK   rejected_program_names_its_own_word" else "plant: a rejected program must be told apart from a stale line"
assert control.out contains "OK   rejected_program_leaves_no_destination" else "plant: a rejected program must write no destination"

# plant_apply: in place, and the mode is tracked content.
assert control.out contains "OK   apply_lands" else "plant: an in-place plant must reach the file"
assert control.out contains "OK   apply_refuses_a_stale_line" else "plant: an in-place plant matching nothing must refuse"
assert control.out contains "OK   refused_apply_leaves_the_file_byte_identical" else "plant: a refused in-place plant must leave the file untouched"
assert control.out contains "OK   apply_keeps_the_exec_bit" else "plant: writing through the original inode is what keeps a tracked mode"
assert control.out contains "OK   apply_left_no_temporary" else "plant: a plant must leave no temporary in the pen"
assert control.out contains "OK   write_to_a_new_destination_keeps_the_exec_bit" else "plant: a new destination is seeded with cp, so the source mode travels without asking stat"

# The load-bearing leg -- the defect asserted, not only the repair.
assert control.out contains "OK   the_strip_plant_landed" else "plant: the plant into the helper copy must itself land, or phase 4 tests nothing"
assert control.out contains "OK   stripped_helper_reads_a_no_op_as_landed" else "plant: stripped of its comparison the helper must read a no-op as landed -- that is the defect this rung exists for"
assert control.out contains "OK   stripped_helper_left_the_file_unmutated" else "plant: the stripped helper's victim must stand unmutated, proving the reading was the only thing removed"

# The real tree, not only pen text.
assert control.out contains "OK   real_source_plant_lands" else "plant: the helper must work on a tracked source"
assert control.out contains "OK   real_source_stale_plant_refuses" else "plant: a stale line in a tracked source must refuse"

say "field GREEN -- a plant that plants nothing says so by name, and the stripped helper proves the saying is load-bearing"

let adoption = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/plant_adoption_scan.sh"]
assert adoption.ok else "plant: the adoption scan must balance -- read its own lines"
say adoption.out

# A FLOOR THAT ONLY RISES, which is the mirror of this tree's usual ratchet. The population counted
# here is the good one, so the number moves the other way: raise it whenever a lane adopts, and it
# may never fall. Seated at 4 on 20260907 -- the three Mantra controls that met the fault, plus the
# helper's own control. RAISED TO 5 on 20260907 by the research lane, whose
# `tools/fixtures/t/topology_growth_control.sh` was written against the law rather than repaired
# into it: the first control to adopt at birth rather than on touch. RAISED TO 7 on
# `20260907.062519` by BAKERY, when the recovered `index_shelf_repair_control.sh` and
# `standing_equipment_scope_rank_control.sh` landed sourcing it. RAISED TO 9 on `20260907.093000`
# by two lanes landing in one hour: `foundations_link_control.sh`, which came back out of a stash
# sourcing it to prove that two copies of a scan differ from the source they were cut from, and
# `mantra_declaration_walk_control.sh`, out of that same dead-letter box, adopted because its own
# elder-ArrayList plant had gone stale -- naming `u32` after that type became `LineId`, which is
# the exact fault the helper exists to name. RAISED AGAIN on `20260907.081756` by BAKERY, by two
# more, and they are worth telling apart. One is the usual on-touch fall:
# `seat_prompt_figure_control.sh` reached for `plant_apply` because a `sed -i` in it had broken
# `shell_dialect`'s ceiling of zero, so the FIRST site this floor rose by was a guard rather than a
# hand. The other, `scope_trace_control.sh`, adopted at birth. The remaining controls are named by
# `sh tools/fixtures/p/plant_adoption_scan.sh --list`, and each falls on touch.
# RAISED AGAIN on `20260907.111058` by DIFFUSER, and by the same door BAKERY's first site came
# through: `topology_relaxed_control.sh` was born with eleven `sed -i` plants, `shell_dialect`
# refused the hot pass at its ceiling of zero, and the portable spelling this law already owned was
# the repair. The second gain was the one the law is actually for -- one of those eleven plants had
# been rewriting the checker's own string literals and proving nothing, which `plant_apply` names.
# RAISED AGAIN on `20260907.153000` by DIFFUSER: `topology_occupied_control.sh` was born sourcing the
# plant law, by the same sibling door -- a control that plants a fault into a copy of its own scan
# and lifts it again wants the portable spelling from its first line rather than on its first refusal.
assert adoption.out contains "sourcing=13" else "plant: adoption is a floor that only rises -- thirteen controls source the plant law; raise this line when a lane adopts, never lower it"
assert adoption.out contains "verdict=ok" else "plant: the adoption arithmetic must sum before it is believed"

say "plant: GREEN -- one implementation, imported by thirteen controls, proven from both sides on metal"
